41. Financial Ownership Rule

The ownership hierarchy is:

Chama
   │
   ▼
Membership
   │
   ├── Contribution
   ├── Share
   ├── Loan
   ├── Loan Repayment
   └── Payout

Payment infrastructure then records how money moved:

Business Record
      │
      ▼
Payment
      │
      ▼
Payment Attempt
      │
      ▼
Provider Transaction
      │
      ▼
Bank Transaction
      │
      ▼
Reconciliation
      │
      ▼
Ledger

Not every payment will necessarily have every record in this chain.

---

42. Monetary Data

All money uses:

NUMERIC(14,2)

and Python:

Decimal

Never:

float

for financial amounts.

Examples:

1000.00 KES
25000.00 KES
150000.50 KES

---

43. Dates and Times

Use timezone-aware timestamps where appropriate.

Application code should consistently handle:

datetime

using timezone-aware values.

Business dates such as:

contribution_date

may use "DATE" when a time of day is not meaningful.

---

44. Foreign Keys

Relationships must use foreign keys.

Example:

memberships.member_id
        ↓
members.id

and:

memberships.chama_id
        ↓
chamas.id

Do not store relationships only as arbitrary strings.

Bad:

member_name = "John"

Better:

member_id = UUID

---

45. Deletion Rules

Do not cascade-delete financial history accidentally.

For example, deleting a membership should not silently delete:

Contributions
Loans
Repayments
Payments
Ledger Entries

Financial history must remain traceable.

Where a member leaves a Chama, prefer:

membership.status = EXITED

rather than deleting the historical membership.

---

