47. Models Can Be Prepared Early

It is acceptable to define future SQLAlchemy models in the source tree so developers understand the complete domain.

However:

Model exists in Python

does NOT automatically mean:

Table exists in database

Future tables should not be migrated until their roadmap version is active.

---

48. Database Reset During Development

Because SQLite is being used during development, developers may reset the database when appropriate.

Example:

rm chamacore.db
alembic upgrade head

This is acceptable for local development.

It is not acceptable for staging or production.

---

49. Migration Rules

Every schema change must have an Alembic migration.

Example:

alembic revision --autogenerate -m "create members and memberships"

Then:

alembic upgrade head

Developers must review generated migrations instead of blindly trusting "--autogenerate".

